  {
    "sha": "806aa0cf9ddcb82c087603e0fc45c08ffa57f2c4",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDgwNmFhMGNmOWRkY2I4MmMwODc2MDNlMGZjNDVjMDhmZmE1N2YyYzQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T14:56:00Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-20T14:56:00Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(cl): the clearance plane must clear the stock and the fixtures for the first traverse\n\nThe opening rapid of a clearance-seeded milling path starts over its own\nentry (edd41f0f5), so no invented line from the WCS origin reaches the\ntoolpath, the CL, the simulation or the fixture checks. The first\ntraverse after a tool change comes from an X/Y the machine does not\nknow, so a new law (sim::verify::first_traverse_low, verdict\nWarning::FirstTraverseLow) requires the path's start height to stand at\nor over the start stock's top and every fixture's top, in the\noperation's frame (3+2 reads along its tool axis; the machine table slab\nis read upright only). A start under either top holds the post by name\nand says to raise the clearance height. Rotary, multi-axis and cross\ndrill kinds are #2965.\n\nThe op stamp salt moves to v4. The example projects first-4axis-part,\nfirst-continuous-4axis-part, first-router-part and guide-multiaxis are\nregenerated through the app's load, generate and save path; no\ncommitted .nc changes. Eight CL goldens change only their START line.\nDecision: docs/decisions/2901-first-traverse-law.md.\n\nFixes #2901\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
