      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T15:34:09Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): judge the first traverse of a 3+2 plane against the machine table\n\nA 3+2 plane read no machine table, so a head-tilt clearance plane that\ndrops under the table top inside the travel passed. The law now reads the\ntable's top face over the stated travel when the head tilts. It does not\nread the table when only the work tilts (each tilting rotary turns the\npart), because the table stays under the work there. A mounted machine\nthat states no travel gives a note that names the table as not judged.\n\nFixes #2987\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
